        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0b483907-8bd3-53d3-ac78-cbb30861ee8b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Carsten Erik Olsen; S. P. L. Sørensen\n- Organizations: Carlsberg Laboratory\n- Roles: plant ecologist; plant physiologist; chemist\n- Concepts: plant nutrition; soil pH; pH scale; acidity; alkalinity\n\nFacts:\n- S. P. L. Sørensen was a Danish chemist who introduced the concept of pH as a scale for measuring acidity and alkalinity.\n- Carsten Erik Olsen was a Danish plant ecologist and plant physiologist who pioneered the study of plant nutrition in soils of different pH.\n- Carsten Erik Olsen worked at the Carlsberg Laboratory as an assistant to S. P. L. Sørensen and later had his own laboratory there.",
